.TH ROLLING_CONFIG 8 "2026-11-20" "rolling-linux 2.1.11" "Rolling WWAN Services Manual"
.SH NAME
rolling_config \- firmware configuration service for Rolling Wireless WWAN devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/bin/rolling_config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rolling_config
is the OEM configuration service of the Rolling Linux apps set for WWAN
devices.  It is started by
.BR systemd (1)
as
.B rolling_config.service
and runs as a system daemon; it is not normally started by hand.
.PP
On start-up the service reads the OEM\-specific configuration file
.B rwwwanConfig.ini
(seeded into
.IR /etc/rolling/config_file/rolling_config_service/ ,
see
.BR rwwwanConfig.ini (5)),
applies it to the WWAN modem and publishes the running configuration
to the other Rolling services through the
.B rolling_helper
D\-Bus service (see
.BR rolling_helper (8)).
.PP
A configuration reload can be requested by sending the service a SIGHUP
(systemctl reload rolling_config.service).
.SH OPTIONS
.B rolling_config
takes no command\-line options; it is managed through systemd and the
configuration file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rolling/config_file/rolling_config_service/rwwwanConfig.ini
Runtime configuration.  Seeded from the shipped templates at install
time or first boot, and never overwritten afterwards, so local edits
survive upgrades.
.TP
.I /usr/share/linux\-apps/config_set/<project>_<oem>/
Per\-OEM configuration templates shipped by the package.
.TP
.I /var/lib/rolling/run
Runtime state directory (created by the package post\-install script).
.SH SYSTEMD
.B rolling_config.service
is ordered after
.B ModemManager.service
and
.BR rolling_helper.service .
ExecReload re\-reads the configuration on SIGHUP.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
systemctl daemon\-reload
systemctl enable rolling_config.service
systemctl start rolling_config.service
systemctl status rolling_config.service
systemctl reload rolling_config.service
systemctl stop rolling_config.service
.fi
.PP
Watch the service journal:
.nf
journalctl \-u rolling_config.service
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rolling_flash (8),
.BR rolling_helper (8),
.BR rolling_ma (8),
.BR rwwwanConfig.ini (5),
.BR systemd (1)
